{"name":"Metal Flake","hex":"#838782","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"metal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Chemical elements or alloys, their ores, and the mines where their ores come from.\n Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity.\n\n Any material with similar physical properties as those chemical elements, especially as a combination of several of them, such as an alloy.\n\n An element which was not directly created after the Big Bang but instead formed through nuclear reactions; any element other than hydrogen and helium.\n\n Crushed rock, stones etc. used to make a road.\n\n The ore from which a metal is derived.\n A mine from which ores are taken.","Any of a number of chemical elements in the periodic table that form a metallic bond with other metal atoms; generally shiny, somewhat malleable and hard, often a conductor of heat and electricity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by strong drum-beats and distorted guitars. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Having the emotional or social characteristics associated with metal music; brash, bold, frank, unyielding, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/metal"},{"term":"flake","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A loose filmy mass or a thin chiplike layer of anything","A scale of a fish or similar animal"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To break or chip off in a flake.","To prove unreliable or impractical; to abandon or desert, to fail to follow through."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Metallic paint","blocks":[{"text":"Metallic paint, which may also be called metal flake, is a type of paint that is most common on new automobiles, but is also used for other purposes. Metallic paint can reveal the contours of bodywork more than non-metallic, or \"solid\" paint. Close-up, the small metal flakes included in the paint create a sparkling effect mimicking a metal surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/1967_Green_Ford_Thunderbird_Fordor.jpg/330px-1967_Green_Ford_Thunderbird_Fordor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metallic_paint","wikidata":"Q1427865"},{"title":"Metal","blocks":[{"text":"A metal is a material that, when polished or fractured, shows a lustrous appearance, and conducts electricity and heat relatively well. These properties are all associated with having electrons available at the Fermi level, as opposed to nonmetallic materials which do not. Metals are typically ductile and malleable."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg/330px-Iron_electrolytic_and_1cm3_cube.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Metal","wikidata":"Q11426"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/68custom.jpg/500px-68custom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/68custom.jpg/1280px-68custom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/68custom.jpg/500px-68custom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1968 Camaro Custom with metal flake paint. Size and reflectivity of flakes seen on this custom paint job is higher than conventional metallic paint.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A68custom.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Compo_EasyRider_HD_Captain_America_und_Billy_Bike_noBG.jpg/500px-Compo_EasyRider_HD_Captain_America_und_Billy_